    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0047" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Colombia/612: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-22T16:00:00-05:00">March 22, 1943—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>510. Department’s telegram 357, March 20, 7 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d38-f1"/>
                    Complete preliminary agreement has been reached with the Minister of War<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d38-f2"/> on the air rubber agreement based on terms
                    conforming with the original contract submitted by Defense Supplies Corporation.
                    To <pb facs="0048" n="34" xml:id="pg34"/> simplify procedure Colombian
                    authorities have considered it advisable to put this agreement into effect as
                    one of the individual steps to be taken in the implementation of the more
                    general agreement on strategic materials concerning which the exchange of notes
                    referred to in the Embassy’s telegram 495, March 19, 3 p.m.<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d38-f3"/> and previous correspondence is pending. It is expected
                    that the air rubber agreement will be made effective after such exchange of
                    notes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d38-f1" n="66" xml:id="d38-f1-content">
